From: RCTools GPU audit
Subject: [PATCH EXPERIMENTAL] readback: pipeline two PBOs for eglkgsl mono X11

Base: VirtualGL/virtualgl 2473cf39bdbe88ca41ecd58ac4007385c9682a9f
Requires: virtualgl-kgsl-pack-invert.experimental.patch

Add an opt-in VGL_KGSL_PBO_PIPELINE=1 path for the project-specific eglkgsl
backend.  It is intentionally restricted to full-frame mono X11 readback with
GL_MESA_pack_invert active.  The first frame warms the pipeline synchronously.
Subsequent calls copy the previous PBO before enqueueing the current glReadPixels
into the other PBO, introducing one frame of latency while avoiding the
upstream same-PBO immediate-map serialization.

Any layout/read-buffer change resets and reallocates both PBO stores.  Context
recreation invalidates the PBO names.  All other paths retain VirtualGL's
existing synchronous/PBO behavior.

This patch is source-only until real FD506/TigerVNC A/B testing validates
correctness, latency, and performance.

